{"availability":"available","full":"ondmindmanagement-hub/bolt-agent-control-plane","name":"bolt-agent-control-plane","description":"Governed AI-agent execution prototype for Nebius x NVIDIA hackathon","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-04T17:31:02Z","updated":"2026-10-10T21:19:24Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://ondmindmanagement-hub.github.io/bolt-agent-control-plane/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-13T07:36:37.038Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-13T07:36:37.038Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-13T07:36:37.038Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T22:06:46.972Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-13T07:36:37.038Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Nebius x NVIDIA Global AI Hackathon 2026 — existing Devpost submission","BOLT Agent Control Plane is an open-source developer-workflow experiment from Omar Baró / Unfire. It separates an AI model's proposed actions from authority to execute them: the language model proposes, and a fixed local policy decides whether a proposed action is allowed, needs human approval, or is denied. This public experiment does not execute system tools, send emails, deploy code or grant actual human approvals.","State as of 9 October 2026: Devpost acknowledged an initial submission on 4 October. This repository was subsequently adapted for Veles Hack (see VELESRESULTS.md). The original source had an isolated Nebius request script and a separate local policy gate. This update connects the Nebius response with the policy gate in code. We tested this new connection using mock API responses, not a new live Nebius inference call. Evidence from a previous Nemotron Playground session is historical."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ondmindmanagement-hub/bolt-agent-control-plane/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"1a7fcf7c70dcff55bb07d3152e9951271dd192df28d5